troglodytic existence, having entered the Dungeons mainly to feign a
knowledge of geology in order to impress its 7-INT spouse.  When you
#chat with it, it complains about the accomodations, and (if female)
the availability of cosmetics.  Most common in Minetown and the
Minesend with all the booze.  Probably wearing a leather jacket,
carrying a can of grease (for the hair), and some gold.  Can be tamed
or pacified by being thrown !oBooze.

Also, since it's so good at keeping time, it would be fast, and
(maybe) grant that intrinsic, as well as exercising dexterity, when
eaten.  Likely to spawn with an instrument (especially fire horns,
which naturally lead to loads of wacky fun for low-albedo protection
racketeers), and tends use it to beat monsters over the head in a
constant, staccato rhythm.

Unfortunately, all that ticking usually manifests itself as extremely
loud footsteps.  Thus a Metro Gnome will create noise as if wearing
Boots of Fumbling, and probably aggravate monsters along the way.

Maybe sacrificing a Metro Gnome would also have a chance of revealing
part of the Castle tune.

